    <string name="c10_description">A bow recalls the archer. Its official sky area lies between Pisces and Cygnus in this selection, so those neighbours make useful comparison practice.</string>
    <string name="c10_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c10_meaning">Archer</string>
    <string name="c10_name">Sagittarius</string>
    <string name="c11_description">The swan takes up a little over eight hundred square degrees. It is only slightly larger in area than Taurus, despite their very different emblems.</string>
    <string name="c11_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c11_meaning">Swan</string>
    <string name="c11_name">Cygnus</string>
    <string name="c12_description">The bull is a strong visual cue for an area just below eight hundred square degrees. Keep its near tie with Cygnus in mind during a wider run.</string>
    <string name="c12_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c12_meaning">Bull</string>
    <string name="c12_name">Taurus</string>
    <string name="c13_description">An eagle marks this constellation. It has a considerably smaller footprint than the swan, showing why an emblem alone cannot tell you how much sky a region holds.</string>
    <string name="c13_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c13_meaning">Eagle</string>
    <string name="c13_name">Aquila</string>
    <string name="c14_description">The scales form a natural reminder to compare quantities carefully. This region covers more sky than Gemini, Cancer or Scorpius, while remaining below Aquila.</string>
    <string name="c14_emoji">⚖️</string>
    <string name="c14_meaning">Scales</string>
    <string name="c14_name">Libra</string>
    <string name="c15_description">A paired figure recalls the twins. Its area sits just above Cancer, a close pairing that rewards learning the measurements rather than judging the emblem size.</string>
    <string name="c15_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c15_meaning">Twins</string>
    <string name="c15_name">Gemini</string>
    <string name="c16_description">The crab names a region just over five hundred square degrees. Its area is slightly greater than Scorpius; both belong to the smaller half of this curated selection.</string>
    <string name="c16_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c16_meaning">Crab</string>
    <string name="c16_name">Cancer</string>
    <string name="c17_description">The scorpion gives this region a memorable emblem. It covers just under five hundred square degrees, below Cancer but comfortably above Aries.</string>
    <string name="c17_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c17_meaning">Scorpion</string>
    <string name="c17_name">Scorpius</string>
    <string name="c18_description">The ram occupies a smaller sky region than many other zodiac emblems. Its measured area still exceeds Capricornus, a useful pair for a close judgement.</string>
    <string name="c18_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c18_meaning">Ram</string>
    <string name="c18_name">Aries</string>
    <string name="c19_description">A goat stands in for the traditional sea goat. This constellation covers a little over four hundred square degrees, noticeably less than the larger water bearer.</string>
    <string name="c19_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c19_meaning">Sea goat</string>
    <string name="c19_name">Capricornus</string>
    <string name="c1_description">A long, winding water snake gives this constellation its emblem. Its boundary encloses the largest area of any constellation, a useful anchor for every comparison in this collection.</string>
    <string name="c1_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c1_meaning">Water snake</string>
    <string name="c1_name">Hydra</string>
    <string name="c20_description">The stringed instrument is a symbolic stand-in for the lyre. This is the smallest region in the twenty-item selection, though many constellations outside the collection are smaller.</string>
    <string name="c20_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c20_meaning">Lyre</string>
    <string name="c20_name">Lyra</string>
    <string name="c2_description">The maiden occupies an enormous stretch of sky. Its area is only slightly smaller than Hydra, making this one of the closest comparisons in the index.</string>
    <string name="c2_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c2_meaning">Maiden</string>
    <string name="c2_name">Virgo</string>
    <string name="c3_description">The great bear has a sky footprint far larger than the familiar ladle-shaped pattern within it. Compare the whole official region, rather than just the stars that catch your eye.</string>
    <string name="c3_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c3_meaning">Great bear</string>
    <string name="c3_name">Ursa Major</string>
    <string name="c4_description">Cetus represents a sea creature in the constellation tradition. The whale emblem is a memory aid for a region whose measured span exceeds twelve hundred square degrees.</string>
    <string name="c4_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c4_meaning">Sea monster</string>
    <string name="c4_name">Cetus</string>
    <string name="c5_description">A winged horse names this broad celestial region. Its footprint belongs among the giants in this selection, even though the emblem itself is compact.</string>
    <string name="c5_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c5_meaning">Winged horse</string>
    <string name="c5_name">Pegasus</string>
    <string name="c6_description">The dragon stretches through a large region of the northern sky. Its area gives a useful step down from Pegasus when learning the relative size of these emblems.</string>
    <string name="c6_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c6_meaning">Dragon</string>
    <string name="c6_name">Draco</string>
    <string name="c7_description">The water bearer is remembered here by a pouring vessel. Its official boundary covers just under a thousand square degrees, a handy middle anchor among the larger entries.</string>
    <string name="c7_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c7_meaning">Water bearer</string>
    <string name="c7_name">Aquarius</string>
    <string name="c8_description">The lion names a generous region of sky. In an area comparison it sits below Aquarius and above Pisces; the brightness of its stars does not change this ordering.</string>
    <string name="c8_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c8_meaning">Lion</string>
    <string name="c8_name">Leo</string>
    <string name="c9_description">The fishes are represented by a single fish emblem for quick recognition. Their constellation spans substantially more sky than smaller zodiac regions such as Aries.</string>
    <string name="c9_emoji">��</string>
    <string name="c9_meaning">Fishes</string>
    <string name="c9_name">Pisces</string>
